! mcp_bootstrap_p104.strap -- printed page 104:
! "******** MCP PSEUDO OPS ********".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.111, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID
! CB000001  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 104".  The TIME CLOCK
! is the same 00054041 every page since p.97 prints, and the PUNID
! is the 11D11MCP that printed p.99 line 13's PUNID card set.  (The
! middle character of the PUNID and the two letters of the card-ID
! prefix sit squarely in this drum's O/C/D failure class; the PUNID
! is read as D because p.99's PUNID CARD is what produced it.  The
! card-ID prefix is read "CB" and is NOT claimed with confidence --
! nothing depends on it.)
!
! FORTY-EIGHT LINES, AND THAT IS COUNTED, NOT ESTIMATED.  The
! rightmost column prints one card serial per line, CB000001 through
! CB000048, forty-eight rows, and the printed line numbers run 1 to
! 48 with no gap.  Below line 48 the page is blank.
!
! >>> THE WHOLE PAGE IS DEFINITIONS AND NOT ONE CARD COMPILES A
! WORD. <<<  Twenty-three SYN cards define twenty-three symbols;
! nineteen more SYN cards are COMMENTED OUT; five cards are the
! heading block; one card is an SLC.  23 + 19 + 5 + 1 = 48.
! So this deck's entire check surface is TWENTY-THREE SYMBOLS AND
! ZERO LISTING ROWS -- printed p.99's convention: a SYN deposits no
! storage word, so it is checked in !SYM and must NOT be faked into
! a !CHECK.  There are no !CHECK lines below and that is correct.
!
! >>> WHAT THE PAGE IS. <<<  It is the MCP PSEUDO-OPERATION CODE
! TABLE: the symbols by which MCP's own code names the pseudo-ops a
! problem program requests with "B,$MCP / ,$<OP> / ...".  Each code
! is a word.bit pair; a word holds four codes at bits .0, .01, .32
! and .33, and the ".01"/".33" neighbour of a code is its "S"
! (suppress-wait) variant.  D RD is 1.0 and D RD S is 1.01; D W is
! 1.32 and D W S is 1.33; and so on through D CHEX at 12.0.
!
! >>> THE NAMES ARE CORROBORATED BY A PRIMARY SOURCE. <<<
! docs/C22-6678-1_7030_MCP_Reference_Jun64.pdf, APPENDIX A, "MCP
! PSEUDO-OPERATION CODES", printed p.42, lists the mnemonic and
! absolute codes available to the problem program.  Its names, in
! order, are
!   $RD $RDS $W $WS $CCW $REL $RELS $LOC $LOCS $FC $FCS $TIF $TIFS
!   $ERG $ERGS $SP $SPS $BSP $BSPS $SPFL $SPFLS $BSFL $BSFLS $WEF
!   $WEFS $REW $REWS $UNLD $UNLDS $RLF $RLFS $RLN $RLNS $KLN $KLNS
!   $FREE $GONG $GONGS $WAIT $CHEX $IODEF ...
! -- the same names in the same order as this page's NAME column,
! position for position, with the "$" where this page writes "D ".
! That settles by document every glyph on this page that shape alone
! cannot: D CCW (not OCW), D LOC and D LOC S (an O, not a C), D GONG
! and D GONGS, and D CHEX.  The last is confirmed a second time in
! prose: J22-6559 MCP Users Guide printed p.(OCR line 713) says "The
! pseudo-operation $CHEX, Change I-O Tables of Exits".
!
! HOW FAR THE ORACLE REACHES, EXACTLY.  The appendix's NAME column
! OCRs cleanly; its NUMBER column is garbled for the first thirteen
! entries and clean from there on.  The clean tail is twenty-three
! numbers ending in 10.32, and counting back twenty-three names from
! $FREE aligns them: $ERG 5.0, $ERGS 5.01, $SP 5.32, $SPS 5.33,
! $BSP 6.0, $BSPS 6.01, $SPFL 6.32, $SPFLS 6.33, $BSFL 7.0, $BSFLS
! 7.01, $WEF 7.32, $WEFS 7.33, $REW 8.0, $REWS 8.01, $UNLD 8.32,
! $UNLDS 8.33, $RLF 9.0, $RLFS 9.01, $RLN 9.32, $RLNS 9.33, $KLN
! 10.00, $KLNS 10.01, $FREE 10.32.  Every one of those agrees with
! this page.  The CODES for $RD..$TIFS (1.0 .. 4.01) rest on THIS
! page's own LOCATION column and the .0/.01/.32/.33 pattern, not on
! the manual.  And D TIN (4.32) and D TINS (4.33) have NO Appendix A
! entry at all -- the appendix jumps $TIFS -> $ERG.  Both are
! comment cards here so nothing depends on them, but the absence is
! recorded rather than passed over; the 1964 appendix is a later
! revision of a different document than this March 1963 listing.
!
! >>> THE CHECK THE PAGE PERFORMS ON ITSELF. <<<  Each SYN prints
! its bit offset in DECIMAL in the STATEMENT column and the same
! offset in OCTAL in the LOCATION column, and all twenty-three
! agree: 1.32/000001.40, 1.33/000001.41, 8.0/000010.00,
! 9.33/000011.41, 10.32/000012.40, 11.32/000013.40, 12.0/000014.00
! and the rest.  That is a real check of the digits, though not of
! the card.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS AND OMISSIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) LINE 6'S CARD IS "SLC,$" AND THIS DECK WRITES
!     "SLC, (8)215020.71".  The page prints the location 215020.71
!     against that card.  In an isolated deck "$" is zero, not
!     0o215020.71, so transcribing the card verbatim would record a
!     different fact than the page does; the printed location is
!     written instead and the printed card is recorded here
!     verbatim.  strap_asm DOES accept a bare "SLC, $" -- this is a
!     deliberate substitution, not an assembler limitation.  It is
!     documentary only: nothing on this page emits a storage word,
!     so no symbol and no bit depends on the origin.
!     The bit offset is written .71 EXACTLY AS PRINTED, because
!     inside an (8) literal both parts are base 8.
!     >>> AND IT COSTS ONE CHECK, SO IT IS SAID OUT LOUD. <<<  A
!     HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE WITH THE ARRIVING COUNTER -- it
!     overrides it silently.  When printed pp.100-103 land, the
!     counter they leave behind must be compared BY HAND against
!     this page's printed 215020.71, and this SLC reconsidered (a
!     bare "SLC,$" would then make the join self-checking).  Until
!     then this line is the one place in this deck where an error
!     could hide, and nothing else here depends on it.
!
! (2) THE FIVE HEADING CARDS (lines 1-5) ARE NOT TRANSCRIBED: 1 and
!     5 are blank comment cards, 2 and 4 are rules of asterisks and
!     3 is "******** MCP PSEUDO OPS ********".
!
! (3) THE NINETEEN COMMENTED-OUT SYN CARDS ARE NOT TRANSCRIBED.
!     THEY ARE IDENTIFIED BY TWO TELLS, AND THE DASH IS NOT ONE OF
!     THEM:
!       (i)  LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT are BOTH empty, and
!       (ii) the fields DO NOT LINE UP with the rows above.  A card
!            that assembles is printed field by field and aligns; a
!            comment is printed as a RAW CARD IMAGE from column 2
!            on, so nothing aligns.  Here the image starts ONE
!            CHARACTER right of the NAME column, and the raw print
!            runs the fields together where the card is wide: lines
!            29, 33, 37 and 46 print "DSPFLS", "DWEFS", "DUNLDS",
!            "DGONGS" closed up against the D, and line 31 prints
!            "D BSFLSSYN,7.01" with NO GAP before SYN.  No compiled
!            row on this page does either; all twenty-three print
!            NAME and STATEMENT in their own columns.
!     THE DASH IS WEAK EVIDENCE AND IS NOT RELIED ON.  Every one of
!     these nineteen cards does print a "-" at that position, and so
!     do lines 1-5, but that column is simply CARD COLUMN 2 OF THE
!     RAW IMAGE: it holds a "-" on some comment cards and a blank on
!     others.  Measured elsewhere in this same assembly -- printed
!     p.101 line 2 is unambiguously a comment card
!     ("-***** UNIT AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS *****-", empty LOCATION,
!     empty BINARY) and prints NO dash there at 1200 dpi while lines
!     1, 3 and 4 of the same box do.  So the dash is recorded as an
!     observation, and tells (i) and (ii) are what the nineteen
!     rests on.
!     They are, with the code each would have defined:
!       line 13 D RELS 2.33    line 16 D FC   3.32
!       line 17 D FCS  3.33    line 18 D TIF  4.0
!       line 19 D TIFS 4.01    line 20 D TIN  4.32
!       line 21 D TINS 4.33    line 22 D ERG  5.0
!       line 25 D SPS  5.33    line 27 D BSPS 6.01
!       line 29 DSPFLS 6.33    line 31 D BSFLS 7.01
!       line 33 DWEFS  7.33    line 35 D REWS 8.01
!       line 37 DUNLDS 8.33    line 38 D RLF  9.0
!       line 40 D RLN  9.32    line 45 D GONG 11.0
!       line 46 D GONGS 11.01
!     NONE of them is faked into a !SYM: a commented card defines
!     nothing, so there is nothing to check.
!
! (4) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.  The NAME column prints "D RD", "D RD S", "D W", "D W S",
!     "D CCW", "D REL", "D LOC", "D LOC S", "D ERG S", "D SP",
!     "D BSP", "D SPFL", "D BSFL", "D WEF", "D REW", "D UNLD",
!     "D RLF S", "D RLN S", "D KLN", "D KLN S", "D FREE", "D WAIT",
!     "D CHEX".
!
! (5) NOTHING ELSE.  strap_asm refused no printed spelling and no
!     printed operand on this page.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE GLYPHS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIS PAGE OPENS ROUND GLYPHS FREELY, and it proves it in ENGLISH
! on its own line 3: the heading "MCP PSEUDO OPS" renders at 1200
! dpi as "MCP PSEUDC CPS" -- the O of PSEUDO and the O of OPS both
! print with the right side broken, beside a C in MCP that looks the
! same.  So shape alone decides nothing here, which is exactly why
! Appendix A is cited above rather than a zoom.
!
! EVERY LOCATION ON THIS PAGE IS AN OCTAL FIELD, printed
! "0000NN.NN+", and a round glyph there is a 0 with certainty: line
! 7 renders as "00C001.C0+", line 11 as "000002.C0+", line 34 as
! "00CC1C.CO+".  All zeros.  The STATEMENT column's bit offsets are
! DECIMAL and three of them print their 0 open -- line 34 "SYN,8.C",
! line 42 "SYN,10.C", line 48 "SYN,12.C" -- and all three are 0,
! confirmed by their own LOCATION fields 000010.00, 000012.00 and
! 000014.00.
!
! THE C/D PAIR GAVE NO TROUBLE IN THE NAME COLUMN: every name's
! leading "D" prints the straight vertical left stem with squared
! corners, plainly unlike the stemless round C of "D CCW" and
! "D CHEX" in the same rows.
!
! >>> NO !CHECK LINE EXISTS ON THIS PAGE, so no byte was read and
! none was disputed.  The BINARY OUTPUT column prints "+00000000"
! and the data description "NULL" on all twenty-three compiled SYN
! cards.  That is the column working correctly on a definitions page
! -- a SYN with no mode has a NULL data description -- and not a
! crop in the wrong place.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY ONE of the forty-eight line numbers carries an asterisk
! right after it ("7*", "48*").  That is the ordinary column, as on
! printed p.99, and is not a mark.  LINE 6 carries a SECOND asterisk
! after its LOCATION, "215020.71 *", which is the familiar mark that
! printed pp.3/37/38/39/88/97/98 also carry.  Line 27's BINARY
! OUTPUT area carries a small solid ink blob; line 27 is a comment
! card with no binary at all, so the blob is a scan artifact and not
! a character.  No mark changes a compiled bit, and this page
! compiles none.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE THE PAGE SITS -- TWO DIFFERENT "LOCATIONS", LABELLED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * THE LOCATION COUNTER.  Line 6 prints 215020.71 and NOTHING on
!   this page emits storage, so the counter leaves the page exactly
!   where it arrived.  Printed p.105 should therefore RESUME at
!   215020.71 -- but that is testable only at p.105's first card
!   that EMITS STORAGE, if it has one.  docs/syn_cards.md records
!   p.105 line 1 as "S FREE SYN,12.22", and a SYN prints a SYMBOL
!   VALUE in the LOCATION column, not a storage location, so line 1
!   cannot test it.  ONE THING IS NOT SETTLED HERE: whether 215020.71 is
!   the counter ON ARRIVAL or the counter AFTER "SLC,$" -- for a
!   "SLC,$" the two are the same value, so this page cannot tell
!   them apart, and p.99's SLC printed its POST-SLC value.  The
!   p.103/p.105 join settles it, not this page.
! * THE SYMBOL VALUES, which is what the LOCATION column actually
!   holds on all twenty-three of these rows: FIRST 000001.00 (line
!   7, D RD) and LAST 000014.00 (line 48, D CHEX).
!   >>> THESE ARE SYN VALUES, NOT ASSEMBLY ADDRESSES. <<<  THERE IS
!   NO ADDRESS CHAIN TO CLOSE ACROSS THIS PAGE and none should be
!   attempted: the location counter does not advance by one bit
!   anywhere on it.  Printed pp.99-102 are the same kind of page.
!   The only address this page states is line 6's 215020.71.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> A LIVE CROSS-DECK COLLISION: DFREE.  REPORTED, NOT FIXED. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Three facts, all independently established:
!   (a) printed p.98 line 27 declares "D FREE SYN,0", location
!       000000.00+, and decks/mcp_bootstrap_p98.strap:172 carries it
!       as "DFREE SYN, 0".
!   (b) printed p.104 line 44 -- THIS page -- declares
!       "D FREE SYN,10.32", location 000012.40+.
!   (c) C22-6678-1 Appendix A gives "$FREE 10.32", agreeing with
!       (b) and not with (a).
! And the IPL deck's own rows prove 0 was in force where they sit:
! printed p.71 line 1, p.75 line 26 and p.97 line 13 each print the
! parameter half-word ",DFREE" as "000000.00 80".  Had DFREE been
! 0o12.40 there, they would have printed 000012.40 80.
!
! WHAT THIS DOES NOT SETTLE.  Whether pp.15-98 and pp.99-onward are
! ONE assembly in which STRAP permits a SYN to be redefined (so that
! DFREE is 0 before line 44 and 10.32 after it), or TWO assemblies
! that merely share a TIME CLOCK.  printed p.99's deck argues for
! one assembly from the location counter never restarting at its
! line 9, which is good evidence but does not rule out redefinition.
! Nothing on p.104 decides it and nothing here pretends to.
!
! WHAT IT MEANS PRACTICALLY: this is a MERGE-TIME COLLISION, not a
! transcription error.  A merged image built from both p.98's deck
! and this one has DFREE declared twice with different values, and
! the symbol-agreement guard will reject it.  That is the
! maintainer's call -- scope the MCP-deck pages separately, or carry
! DFREE as a known divergence.  DFREE is the ONLY one of this page's
! twenty-three names that any other deck in the corpus mentions;
! the other twenty-two appear nowhere else.

        SLC, (8)215020.71           ! line 6 -- printed card is "SLC,$"

